{"name":"Boa","hex":"#7f7755","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Boa","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Boidae – boa constrictors."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of a Bwa-speaking ethnic group of the Democratic Republic of the Congo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Boa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boidae","blocks":[{"text":"The Boidae, commonly known as boas or boids, are a family of nonvenomous snakes primarily found in the Americas, as well as Africa, Europe, Asia, and some Pacific islands. Boas include some of the world's largest snakes, with the green anaconda of South America being the heaviest and second-longest snake known; in general, adults are medium to large in size, with females usually larger than the males. Six subfamilies comprising 14-15 genera and 54-67 species are currently recognized."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Red-tailed_boa_%28Boa_constrictor_constrictor%29_Rio_Napo.jpg/330px-Red-tailed_boa_%28Boa_constrictor_constrictor%29_Rio_Napo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boidae","wikidata":"Q45556"},{"title":"Boinae","blocks":[{"text":"The Boinae are a purported subfamily of boas found in Central and South America, as well as the West Indies. In the Integrated Taxonomic Information System (ITIS), Boinae is considered an invalid synonym of Boidae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Red-tailed_boa_%28Boa_constrictor_constrictor%29_Rio_Napo.jpg/330px-Red-tailed_boa_%28Boa_constrictor_constrictor%29_Rio_Napo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boinae","wikidata":"Q887595"},{"title":"BoA","blocks":[{"text":"Kwon Bo-ah, known professionally as BoA, is a South Korean singer, songwriter, and actress often referred to as the \"Queen of K-pop\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/180417_%EB%B3%B4%EC%95%84_03_%28cropped%29_02.png/330px-180417_%EB%B3%B4%EC%95%84_03_%28cropped%29_02.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BoA","wikidata":"Q232449"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Rudimentary_hindlegs_spurs_in_Boa_constrictor_snake.jpg/500px-Rudimentary_hindlegs_spurs_in_Boa_constrictor_snake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Rudimentary_hindlegs_spurs_in_Boa_constrictor_snake.jpg/1280px-Rudimentary_hindlegs_spurs_in_Boa_constrictor_snake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Rudimentary_hindlegs_spurs_in_Boa_constrictor_snake.jpg/500px-Rudimentary_hindlegs_spurs_in_Boa_constrictor_snake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cloaca region of a Boa constrictor with spurs (rudimentary hindlegs)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARudimentary_hindlegs_spurs_in_Boa_constrictor_snake.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Boavus_idelmani.JPG/500px-Boavus_idelmani.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Boavus_idelmani.JPG/1280px-Boavus_idelmani.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Boavus_idelmani.JPG/500px-Boavus_idelmani.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A fossil of Boavus idelmani, an extinct species of boa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoavus_idelmani.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm